---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Inspect a known Rust position through its explicitly prepared native semantic owner

Usage: pse inspect entity [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>  Exact working Rust file; no editor attachment or unsaved buffer is assumed

Options:
  -C <checkout>

      --line <LINE>
          One-based source line [default: 1]
      --column <COLUMN>
          One-based Unicode scalar column, excluding CR/LF; converted to negotiated encoding [default: 1]
      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices
      --if-source <IF_SOURCE>
          Refuse if the original source digest differs
      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --if-generation <IF_GENERATION>
          Refuse stale generation-bound action selection
      --if-candidate <IF_CANDIDATE>
          Discovery fingerprint for a selected hint/completion/assist; indexes are not identities
      --configuration <CONFIGURATION>
          Require this explicit session configuration identity
      --end-line <END_LINE>
          Inclusive final line for selected inlay/SSR range; defaults to the selected line
      --view <VIEW>
          [default: explain] [possible values: lifetime, compatibility, visibility, format-origin, derive-origin, explain, layout, symbols, refs, calls, implementations, macro, tests, candidates, candidate, hints, hint, predicate, assists]
      --select <SELECT>

      --text <TEXT>

      --compiler-layout <COMPILER_LAYOUT>
          Passively associate an original type-sizes acquisition; requires --view layout
      --compiler-evidence <COMPILER_EVIDENCE>
          Original compiler artifact reference accompanying a lifetime inquiry
      --work-result <WORK_RESULT>
          Original work invocation accompanying the inquiry; no execution association is inferred
      --against-result <AGAINST_RESULT>
          Original guarded position for a native compatibility or visibility comparison
      --operation <OPERATION>
          [possible values: equal, could-unify, could-coerce]
  -h, --help
          Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Inspect a known Rust position through its explicitly prepared native semantic owner

Usage: pse inspect entity [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          Exact working Rust file; no editor attachment or unsaved buffer is assumed

Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --line <LINE>
          One-based source line

          [default: 1]

      --column <COLUMN>
          One-based Unicode scalar column, excluding CR/LF; converted to negotiated encoding

          [default: 1]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated literal top-level payload names (for example records). Dots and slashes do not navigate nested data; schema shows valid choices

      --if-source <IF_SOURCE>
          Refuse if the original source digest differs

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --if-generation <IF_GENERATION>
          Refuse stale generation-bound action selection

      --if-candidate <IF_CANDIDATE>
          Discovery fingerprint for a selected hint/completion/assist; indexes are not identities

      --configuration <CONFIGURATION>
          Require this explicit session configuration identity

      --end-line <END_LINE>
          Inclusive final line for selected inlay/SSR range; defaults to the selected line

      --view <VIEW>
          Possible values:
          - lifetime
          - compatibility
          - visibility
          - format-origin
          - derive-origin
          - explain
          - layout:          Inspect fallible layout with native type/target context
          - symbols
          - refs
          - calls
          - implementations
          - macro
          - tests
          - candidates
          - candidate
          - hints
          - hint
          - predicate
          - assists

          [default: explain]

      --select <SELECT>


      --text <TEXT>


      --compiler-layout <COMPILER_LAYOUT>
          Passively associate an original type-sizes acquisition; requires --view layout

      --compiler-evidence <COMPILER_EVIDENCE>
          Original compiler artifact reference accompanying a lifetime inquiry

      --work-result <WORK_RESULT>
          Original work invocation accompanying the inquiry; no execution association is inferred

      --against-result <AGAINST_RESULT>
          Original guarded position for a native compatibility or visibility comparison

      --operation <OPERATION>
          Possible values:
          - equal:        Exact native type equality in a common owner
          - could-unify:  Possible deep unification, not compiler acceptance
          - could-coerce: Directional possible coercion from selected to against

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
